  {
    "date": "2019-01-05",
    "term": "宝",
    "kana": "たから",
    "meaning": "treasure",
    "level": "N3",
    "pos": ["noun (common) (futsuumeishi)"],
    "priority": ["ichi1", "news1", "nf05"],
    "stratum": "wago",
    "processes": ["compound", "derivation"],
    "headline": "Takara, “treasure”, was analyzed as 高 (taka-, “high”) plus a pluralizing suffix, but the page calls that semantically problematic.",
    "morphemes": [],
    "sources": [
      {
        "quote": "From Old Japanese. First cited to the Man'yōshū of 759 CE. From Proto-Japonic *takara."
      },
      {
        "quote": "Samuel Martin analyzes this as a compound of 高(たか) (taka-, “high”) + 等(ら) (-ra, pluralizing suffix). However, this is semantically problematic, as such a compound would ordinarily refer to “the heights” as a location, and there is no clear means of deriving the sense of “treasure” from the proposed component parts."
      },
      {
        "quote": "Some sources derive this as a compound of 田(た) (ta, “paddy field”) + から (kara, “from”), literally “from the paddy fields”, from the way people value thriving paddy fields as a unique kind of treasure. However, the sense of “from” for から (kara) does not appear until roughly the Heian period, more recent than the first appearance of takara, making this a folk etymology."
      }
    ],
    "examples": [
      {
        "id": 168536,
        "ja": "子供は私の宝です。",
        "en": "My children are my treasures.",
        "enId": 245955,
        "form": "宝",
        "furigana": [
          ["子供", "こども"],
          ["は"],
          ["私", "わたし"],
          ["の"],
          ["宝", "たから"],
          ["です。"]
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": 168850,
        "ja": "子に過ぎたる宝なし。",
        "en": "There is no treasure more precious than a child.",
        "enId": 245640,
        "form": "宝",
        "furigana": [
          ["子", "こ"],
          ["に"],
          ["過", "す"],
          ["ぎたる"],
          ["宝", "たから"],
          ["なし。"]
        ]
      }
    ],
    "wiktionaryDump": "2026-09-02"
  },
