    "processes": [],
    "headline": "Tora is “anomalous”: Old Japanese to₁ra where the expected form was *tura.",
    "morphemes": [],
    "sources": [
      {
        "quote": "From Old Japanese to₁ra, from Proto-Japonic *tora."
      },
      {
        "quote": "Pellard (2013, 92) includes to₁ra among words with o₁ excepted from the /-o-/ to /-u-/ vowel-raising rule and not originating from earlier diphthongs. According to Vovin (2021, 111), West Old Japanese *to₁ra, instead of expected *tura, is \"anomalous\" and possibly \"a case of a sporadic analogical development\"."
      },
      {
        "quote": "Vovin (2013) asserts that this word is same as a Silla place name 刀良 (/*tora/), which matches the Old Japanese phonographic spelling."
      }
    ],
    "examples": [
